  m_text: "massive network continues to be explored, and new passages are still being
    documented. Because of its size, it offers a wide range of geological features
    and hidden rooms. Blue Spring Cave is a favorite among experienced cavers who
    enjoy lengthy, technical expeditions. Its scale demonstrates just how complex
    Tennessee\u2019s underground world can be.\n\n Many Tennessee caves are managed
    with a strong focus on safety and environmental preservation. Visitors must follow
    strict guidelines to protect themselves and the cave ecosystems. These rules
    often include staying on designated paths, avoiding sensitive formations, and
    wearing proper gear. Conservation groups work to monitor cave health and limit
    human impact. Responsible tourism ensures the caves remain beautiful and accessible
    for future generations."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
